#reason test/delegate-e2e-harness.test.ts The project-list test echoed the fixture table back and proved no behaviour.
#reason test/docs-website.test.ts Copy, title and CNAME checks pinned wording and constants, not site behaviour.
#reason test/fix-requests-intent.test.ts The test only repeated the COPY_CHOICES constant it imported.
#reason test/fix-requests-texts.test.ts Snapshots of the English wording and the intent list added no behaviour check.
#reason test/lantern-delegate-messages.test.ts A negative grep of the message table; the unused-key test already catches regressions.
#reason test/lantern-flow-view.test.ts The CSS regex tests tested stylesheet text, not rendered layout.
#reason test/lantern-model.test.ts Doc greps and a policy-file literal duplicated what the floor script tests cover.
#reason test/lantern-own-vocabulary.test.ts A single feature-name check in the map file, not behaviour.
#reason test/lantern-pixi-text-quality.test.ts The 500 ms test asserted a constant the timing tests already use.
#reason test/lantern-plan-messages.test.ts The exit-code table test echoed a constant object.
#reason test/lantern-plan-readability.test.ts CSS text regexes and a sticky-rule grep tested the stylesheet, not the view.
#reason test/lantern-planning-view.test.ts The macOS inset describe was a CSS text check.
#reason test/macro-legend-view.test.ts A negative prose check against old legend wording.
#reason test/macro-sizes-fixture.test.ts Counts of a generated fixture; the drift test already guards it.
#reason test/messages.test.ts A snapshot of English wording duplicated the catalogue itself.
#reason test/scanner.test.ts The timeout test asserted a constant is above 3000.
#reason test/serveweb-launch.test.ts A copy-pasted duplicate test and a grace-time constant check.
#reason test/settings-registry.test.ts Type-only tests that tsc and src typechecking already cover.
#reason test/settings-tabs.test.ts A negative regex on a description string.
#reason test/sidebar.test.ts The scrollbar test grepped CSS text, not behaviour.
#reason test/codex-skill-guides.test.ts Both tests only checked that guide files exist, which the bundle tests already cover.
#story A maintainer runs the unit tests
#step actor Maintainer
#step action runs the unit test suite
#step subject tests that checked only constants and wording
